--- (b) Geohash: scan a cell, then sort what you found ---
    The sort is a real Sort node over every row in the cell. And the
    result is only correct if the 100th nearest point is inside this cell;
    otherwise the query silently returns neighbours that are not the
    nearest. There is no "stop when you have K" -- geohash has no ordering
    by distance, only by cell.
EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)
SELECT location_id, geolocation
FROM locations_gh
WHERE gh LIKE 'dr5ru%'
ORDER BY geolocation <-> POINT(-73.9855, 40.7580)
LIMIT 100;
